    "source": "VortexFPS/VortexMaps",
    "built_by": "build-maps workflow, run 30863556813 (tag maps-2026.08)",
    "pipeline": "q3map2 compile from sources/ + compress-textures + build/publish.py",
    "note": "FIRST release actually produced by this repo's own pipeline. Every earlier release, maps-2026.07 included, was Xonotic's prebuilt xonotic-20230620-maps.pk3 re-split by the now-retired build/split-pack.py bootstrap -- see that tag's provenance block for the byte-identity evidence. Consequently every byte of every map differs from maps-2026.07: lightmaps are not reproducible across compiler runs, and this is a genuine recompile rather than a repackage.",
    "why": "The re-split dropped .waypoints.cache and .waypoints.hardwired -- split-pack.py's SOURCE_EXT classified them as q3map2 residue -- so every shipped map carried bot waypoint NODES with no LINKS and no hand-authored jump/teleport links. Measured on the port's loader: catharsis went 1624 links / 1 dead end -> 1209 / 54, i.e. 29% of its waypoints became nodes a bot can enter and never leave. VortexArena planning/bot-ai-parity-2026-08-03.md D1/D2 has the full analysis.",
    "also_fixed": "sources/ was missing 193 files that existed only inside the shipped archives (32 waypoint caches, 82 ambient .ogg, 36 skybox faces, 30 levelshot minis, 6 cubemaps, 4 models); a rebuild before this would have silently dropped all of them. publish.py now reconciles every dropped file against packlib.KNOWN_DROPS and fails the build on anything unaccounted for.",
    "_init": "Dropped from the set (32 packs -> 31). It is a DarkPlaces boot stub -- a valid world for -listen/-dedicated before a real map loads. Vortex boots through Godot via --host <map>; the only reference left was an inherited startmap_dm alias that nothing invokes."
  },
  "note": "Compiled maps are build output and are not committed (restructure D7). Run tools/data/fetch-maps.py to install them into data/maps/. Packs are .pk3 and are installed as-is, not extracted: MountGameDir mounts a .pk3 natively, so the packed shipping form stays packed (section 9.3). 'shared' carries the art no single map owns; the rest are one per map. truthHash is reserved for the .vmap era, where a bake is content-addressed by the hash of the map's truth sections rather than by a release tag (section 9.4). Rebuilding from source is `python tools/data/fetch-maps.py --rebuild`, which needs the maps-src submodule (`git submodule update --init maps-src`). A rebuild does NOT reproduce the sha256s below and is not meant to: see provenance.evidence -- these packs came from a different producer, and q3map2 output is not byte-reproducible across toolchain versions anyway. --rebuild exists so the map set can be regenerated from sources we control if the release ever goes away, which is the durability guarantee; byte-identity is not part of it.",
